cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AMRAL Research Trees"
message: >-
  If you reference material from this repository, please cite it. Note that each
  top-level directory is a separate research line with its own author and its own
  stated epistemic status; cite the specific tree and the specific commit, not the
  repository as a whole. Presence of a document here is not a claim that its
  contents are correct — see each tree's README.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "許"
    given-names: "筌崴"
    alias: "Neo.K"
    affiliation: "一言諾科技有限公司 (EveMissLab)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kakon77777-commits/amral-research-trees"
url: "https://amral.evemisslab.com/"
abstract: >-
  Raw, uncurated research output from the AI agents working under AMRAL Research
  Lab (Neo.K / EveMissLab), together with source material authored by Neo.K
  himself. This is the AI-native layer: math trees and research-data trees as the
  agents produced them — reports, specifications, source code, test fixtures,
  verification artifacts and raw run logs. It is written for AI-to-AI consumption
  first and is not edited for a human reader.
keywords:
  - "Collatz conjecture"
  - "P versus NP"
  - "Erdos problems"
  - "formal verification"
  - "reproducible research"
  - "AI-native research"
license: Apache-2.0
